FILES YOU DO NOT NEED TO ALTER:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

dut/apb_dummy.sv:
  Dummy APB slave, provides non-trivial data on read cycles
  and reports all active cycles to the console.
  
apb_harness.sv:
  Test harness and test-signals interface, unchanged from the previous exercise 

bases.sv
  Base class definitions for Transaction and Channel classes.
  Transaction is a base class for all transaction data classes
  such as APB_Trans.  Channel is a general-purpose FIFO channel
  that carries Transaction objects from one component to another.
  
apb_tb.sv:
  Top-level test module.  Almost unchanged from the previous answer.


FILES YOU NEED TO WORK ON:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

apb_classes.sv:
  Definitions of classes APB_Trans, APB_Driver, APB_Stim.
  APB_Trans (transaction data) is complete.  APB_Driver and
  APB_Stim are modified versions of the previous driver and stimulus
  generator classes; for this exercise they must have independent
  threads of execution, and communicate using a channel.  You must
  complete these classes by implementing their body() methods.

apb_env.sv:
  Top-level testbench environment class, will have instances of
  APB_Stim and APB_Driver, and a Channel instance to communicate
  between them.  Only a skeleton of this class is provided; you
  must implement it following the pattern shown in the lecture.
